// A standing formation told to re-form where it stands (the player, 2026-11-02: "when I click and drag where they
// stand to tell them to reform where they stand they run in a large arc for a minute just to end in a complete mess"):
// Continental (seed 101, start_epoch 12), the save's mix - 60 halberdiers, 30 grenadiers, 10 diplomats, 4 colossus
// artillery - at 40,40, sent 20 tiles to 40,60 as a deep wedge (autotest formation_kind=4) and left to form, then told
// to form on its middle facing as it stands (a right-button drag of 1 degree: fmove go's facing; the selection takes
// P1's five citizens standing 12 tiles aside too - a few units off the formation are part of it, and so is the ground
// here: the same at 60,60 on open ground didn't show it). `fmove watch 1` logs every unit every step: a reader takes,
// per unit after the drag, the path walked and when it last moved. Found (game_seed 1): with the march's formation set
// ahead (groupmove.c ff_leader, 2026-11-02) the anchor started beyond the leader's spot and came round to it on the
// formation's turning circle - the 109 units walked 27.7 tiles each (max 41.6), the last moving at 128 s, the middle
// 13 tiles south and back; a re-form within the formation's own diameter is no march now (each unit to its place by
// its own route, the game's way) and the set-ahead stops short of the end: 7.3 tiles, the last at 44 s (median 14 s).
// Before the set-ahead (62ea451) 8.4 tiles and 49 s. A drag at the wedge's tip (the formation's radius) is level either
// way (9.1 tiles, 54 s as a march, 64 s in place); 12 tiles and further the march walks what the game's own slots do.
// Later the same day: a formation standing as it marched (the wedge here, formed by the first order) is moved as it
// is by a re-form within its own size - each unit keeps its place, the drag here done at 26.6 s (48.1 before); the
// save's wedge clicked 3 tiles ahead and a bit aside, every unit off the common displacement 0.07 tiles (0.55, 17 of
// 109 by more than a tile, before).
// 2026-11-02, later: the set-ahead replaced by the anchor starting at the mean lag (the slowest units no longer
// behind their places for a whole march): the drag here done at 26.6 s as before, 10 walks back.
wait_until(0.1min)
spawn(1, unit.inf08_halberdier, 40, 40, 60)
spawn(1, unit.inf09_grenadier, 40, 40, 30)
spawn(1, unit.x_diplomat, 40, 40, 10)
spawn(1, unit.gun_artillery13_colossus, 40, 40, 4)
wait_until(0.4min)
cmd("fmove go 1 40 40 14 40 60")
wait_until(1.7min)
cmd("fmove watch 1")
cmd("fmove go 1 40 55 12 40 55 0 1")
every(2s, 1.7min, 4.2min, (run) => {
    cmd("fmove stat")
})
wait_until(4.25min)
cmd("fmove sum")
cmd("fmove watch 0")
